by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-24T07:08:24Z

Thank you for the quick and accurate fix, the root cause analysis was spot on.

While reviewing, I found one case where skipping the static bare accessor changes behavior that predates #65501: a class exposing only a static `foo()` and no other candidate had its `foo` property read through that method since 5.1, and skipping it would turn such reads into a `NoSuchPropertyException` (or resolve to a same-named public property instead of the method). The Serializer is not exposed to that case since `ObjectNormalizer` filters static methods when extracting attributes, but direct PropertyAccess users are.

I reworked the patch to demote instead of skip: a static method named after the property is now tried after all the prefixed accessors, which restores the exact pre-6.4.44 order in every case I probed, including yours. I kept your test and added one covering the last-resort resolution, updated the commit message and the description accordingly, and amended into your commit to preserve authorship.

