by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-24T07:17:40Z

One more refinement after a second look: the previous revision kept the static bare accessor at its historical position, before `__get()` and the property itself. That meant a class exposing both a public `$foo` and a static `foo()` had its property read through the static method, returning a value unrelated to the object's state. That ordering was as questionable as the bug being fixed here, so the static candidate is now tried after every instance-based one, just before giving up. A class exposing only a static `foo()` still resolves to it, so no read that used to work starts throwing.

